        "medicineType": "Emergency Medicine",
        "recordType": "Diagnostic Report",
        "summary": "Lab studies performed in the emergency department on 12/7/2024 revealed a normal complete blood count and differential, including WBC 7.0 (ref 4.0-11.0), Hgb 15.7 (ref 13.5-17.5), and platelet count 274 (ref 150-500). Coagulation studies were within normal limits (PT 10.9 sec, INR 0.97, PTT 29.3 sec). Chemistry panel was notable for a low BUN/Creatinine ratio of 8 (ref 10-20), otherwise electrolytes, renal, and liver function were unremarkable. High-sensitivity troponin was not elevated at 6.5 pg/mL (ref 15.9-38.4). Urine drug screen was negative for amphetamines, barbiturates, benzodiazepines, cannabinoids, cocaine, opiates, PCP, and fentanyl. Ethanol level was elevated at 70 mg/dL (ref &lt;=11). Blood type was O positive and antibody screen was negative. Non-contrast CT of the head performed for moderate to severe head trauma after an MVA showed no acute intracranial process, no hemorrhage, no mass, and no significant chronic changes, but did reveal diffuse thickening of the ethmoid air cells, maxillary sinuses, and sphenoid sinuses consistent with paranasal sinus disease.",
