        "summary": "Subjective: Patient presented for evaluation of left shoulder pain, reporting tenderness over the biceps tendon as well as lateral and posterior shoulder pain.\nObjective: Physical exam confirmed tenderness over the biceps tendon and the lateral/posterior shoulder. X-rays of the left shoulder showed the humeral head was well-centered without fracture, dislocation, or degeneration.\nAssessment: Biceps tendinitis, acute pain, and impingement of the left shoulder.\nPlan: After discussing risks and benefits, the patient requested and received a biceps tendon sheath injection of 40mg Depomedrol, which he tolerated well. Follow-up was scheduled in 3-4 weeks, with a subacromial injection or an MRI considered if pain persisted.",
