        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient was a right-handed truck driver. No specific subjective complaints were documented on these pages.\nObjective: Allergies included fluticasone-salmeterol, ibuprofen, and lorazepam. On physical exam of the left shoulder, there was mild to moderate tenderness in the anterior/posterior shoulder, bicipital groove, and lateral arm. Active and passive range of motion were normal but painful, with forward elevation to 150 degrees and abduction to 140 degrees. Strength was 5/5 but affected by pain. Special tests were positive for Neer's, painful arc, and Speed's.\nAssessment: Left shoulder X-ray showed no acute bony process.\nPlan: The patient received an ultrasound-guided injection of 40 mg methylprednisolone into the left long head of the biceps tendon sheath.",
