        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported persistent, diffuse left shoulder pain since a December 2024 motor vehicle accident. He had received no relief from a prior injection on 07/14/2025 or physical therapy. He denied numbness, tingling, popping, or grinding.\nObjective: Exam of the left shoulder revealed moderate tenderness at the anterior shoulder, lateral arm, and bicipital groove. Range of motion was painful, with abduction past 90 degrees causing pain. Strength was 4/5 for abduction and biceps, limited by pain. Special tests were positive for Neer's, Hawkins, painful arc, and Speed's tests.\nAssessment: Diagnoses included internal derangement and acute pain of the left shoulder.\nPlan: After discussing the lack of relief from the prior injection, the provider recommended a subacromial injection and an MRI to evaluate for a labrum or biceps tendon tear. The patient consented and received a 40mg Depomedrol injection. An order was placed for an MRI of the left shoulder without contrast.",
