        "summary": "Subjective: The 34-year-old male truck driver reported persistent left shoulder pain since a December 2024 motor vehicle accident, with no improvement. He experienced diffuse pain and had no relief from two prior injections or physical therapy.\nObjective: Exam revealed moderate tenderness over the anterior shoulder and lateral arm. Range of motion was normal but painful, and strength was affected by pain. Special tests were positive for painful arc and O'Brien's. An MRI of the left shoulder raised the question of a possible tiny nondisplaced tear of the anterior inferior labrum and showed an intact rotator cuff.\nAssessment: Internal derangement and acute pain of the left shoulder.\nPlan: The MRI findings and treatment options were discussed. A referral was made to Dr. Stepanic for further evaluation of the possible labral tear. A home exercise program was provided.",
