        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for a preoperative evaluation for a left shoulder arthroscopy scheduled for December 1, 2025. He denied any constitutional, ocular, gastrointestinal, skin, or neurological symptoms. Past medical history included asthma and sickle cell-hemoglobin Lepore disease. Past surgical history included a bladder reimplant, ganglion cyst removal, hiatal hernia repair (10/02/2023), and tonsillectomy. He reported never using tobacco, alcohol, or illicit drugs. He had allergies to fluticasone-salmeterol, ibuprofen, and lorazepam, all causing hives.\nObjective: The physical examination was unremarkable.\nAssessment: Pre-op evaluation.\nPlan: A left shoulder orthosis was fitted. Preadmission testing was completed, consent was signed, and a postoperative follow-up was scheduled for approximately five weeks later.",
