        "medicineType": "Radiology",
        "recordType": "Imaging Report",
        "summary": "Body Part: Lumbar spine MRI without contrast. Impression: Multilevel degenerative changes were observed, most prominent at L4-L5 and L5-S1, where focal disc herniations were present. At L4-L5, there was mild interspace narrowing, disc dehydration, posterior disc herniation with a small extruded component, and mild to moderate focal spinal canal stenosis without significant neural foraminal encroachment. At L5-S1, there was mild interspace narrowing, disc dehydration, posterior disc herniation (asymmetrically greater to the left), extruded disc extending into the inferior aspect of the left L5-S1 neural foramen, and neural foraminal stenosis on the left, but the spinal canal remained capacious. Other levels showed mild degenerative changes without significant stenosis, and the conus medullaris and vertebral body heights were unremarkable.",
