        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported ongoing lower back pain, which increased throughout the day to a 7-8/10, and was currently a 6/10. He described the pain as a throbbing, continuous sensation radiating down both legs and into the buttocks, worsened by sitting and bending. He noted his right leg felt cold. The patient also reported right foot pain at 4-5/10, which was exacerbated by physical therapy. He expressed frustration that after six weeks, his back had not improved while his other injuries had. He was taking Mobic, Aleve, and Gabapentin, the latter of which he felt helped slightly.\nObjective: Results of a lumbar spine MRI from 06/07/2023 were reviewed. Findings included multilevel degenerative changes, most prominent at L4-S1. Specific findings included:\n- L4-L5: Central posterior disc herniation with a small extruded component, causing mild to moderate focal spinal canal stenosis.\n- L5-S1: Posterior disc herniation, greater to the left, with an extruded disc extending into the left neural foramen, causing left-sided neural foraminal stenosis.\nAssessment: Lower back strain; multilevel lumbar degenerative changes with disc herniations at L4-L5 and L5-S1.\nPlan: The patient was to continue physical therapy, Mobic, and Gabapentin. He was advised to use ice and continue activity as tolerated.",
