        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for a workers' compensation follow-up for injuries from a 04/12/23 motor vehicle accident where his semi-truck collided with another, causing injuries to his left shoulder, low back, and right leg/knee/ankle. He reported his right knee and left shoulder pain had resolved, but he continued to have low back and right foot pain. He rated his low back pain 6/10, describing it as throbbing and continuous, radiating down both legs to the buttocks. He reported his right foot pain was 4-5/10 and described it as a throbbing, burning sensation. The patient expressed frustration that his other injuries were improving but his back pain was not.\nObjective: Physical examination revealed tenderness in the lumbar spine that radiated laterally, with pain on range of motion and a straight leg raise that caused buttock pain. Neurologic exam showed normal sensory and motor function. A 06/07/23 lumbar spine MRI showed multilevel degenerative changes, most prominent at L4-L5 and L5-S1 with focal disc herniations, mild to moderate spinal canal stenosis at L4-L5, and left neural foraminal stenosis at L5-S1.\nAssessment: Acute lumbar myofascial strain, displaced fracture of the right foot navicular, right ankle sprain, right knee sprain, and left shoulder sprain. The right knee and shoulder sprains were noted as resolved.\nPlan: The provider increased the patient's gabapentin dosage, prescribed tizanidine, and approved physical therapy for the lumbar spine. He was instructed to continue following up with Dr. Pocos for his foot fracture.",
