        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported being unable to drive a truck or perform any lifting. He could sit for one hour before needing to get up and move around.\nObjective: The patient was restricted to working 4 hours per day, 20 hours per week, with these temporary restrictions having started on 04/12/2023. The estimated full duty return-to-work date was 08/08/2023. He had not reached Maximum Medical Improvement (MMI).\nAssessment: Diagnoses included closed navicular fracture of the foot, knee sprain, ankle sprain, shoulder sprain, lower back strain, L4-L5 disc herniation, L5 spinal canal stenosis, and L5-S1 disc herniation.\nPlan: Referrals were made for podiatry, an ankle MRI, neurosurgery, and pain management.",
