        "summary": "First encounter (07/12/2023, Physical Therapy): The patient demonstrated limited lumbar spine flexion range of motion greater than 50% with pain and reported increased pain with sitting, bending, and household work, and was released to return to work on light duty; straight leg raise was positive on the left side. Treatment included 25 minutes of manual therapy (soft tissue mobilization only due to increased pain after sessions), 15 minutes of supervised McKenzie exercise program, 15 minutes of electrical stimulation/cold pack, and 15 minutes of prone mechanical traction at 115#/60#, 60/15. The patient made considerable progress in pain reduction but continued to have pain limiting physical activities and was unable to sit longer than 15 minutes without pain increasing, and felt physical therapy was minimally effective at this point; no further physical therapy was planned unless otherwise advised after consult appointments, and referrals to neurosurgery, pain management, and ankle MRI were being pursued. Second encounter (07/10/2023, Physical Therapy): The patient attended a physical therapy treatment visit supervised by Christine A Pleasnick, PT, with a total treatment time of 55 minutes and 40 minutes of supervised time, but no additional clinical details were provided.",
