        "bodyPart": "Ankle, Shoulder, Knee, Foot, Back, Lower Back",
        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Independent Medical Examination",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient was evaluated in an IME addendum for multiple musculoskeletal injuries, including sprain of the right ankle, left shoulder, right knee, low back strain, displaced dorsum navicular fracture of the right foot, and disc herniations at L4-5 and LS-S1, as well as L4-5 spinal canal stenosis, following an industrial injury on 04/12/2023. The patient's medical records and office visits through 04/18/2023 were reviewed, along with a motion for additional treatment requests dated 07/11/2023. Objective: The IME addendum accepted the objective medical evidence provided by examining physicians but not necessarily their conclusions. Assessment: The provider agreed with the diagnoses of L4-5 disc herniation, L4-5 spinal canal stenosis, and LS-S1 disc herniation based on MRI findings. However, he opined that there was insufficient evidence to relate these conditions to the industrial injury, as the anatomic pain generator had not been clearly identified and clinical findings were associated with a disc herniation at L5-S1, not L4-5, per his evaluation; he recommended that the correct anatomic level be re-addressed after neurosurgery evaluation. Plan: The provider found a podiatry referral for the right foot and ankle medically necessary and appropriate, but did not find a current need for a pain management consult for the right foot and ankle, as MRI results and podiatrist opinion were unknown.",
