        "medicineType": "Occupational Medicine",
        "recordType": "Work Ability Report",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported being unable to drive a truck or lift objects due to ongoing work-related injuries. His allowed conditions included a closed navicular fracture of the foot, knee sprain, ankle sprain, shoulder sprain, and lower back strain, with complicating factors of L4-L5 and S1 disc herniations and spinal canal stenosis.\nObjective: The patient had physical restrictions related to the allowed conditions which were in place since 04/12/2023, and he was not released to return to full duty.\nAssessment: It was determined that the patient had not reached maximum medical improvement (MMI).\nPlan: The patient was to continue medications including meloxicam, tizanidine, and gabapentin and follow up in 6 months. He was also to continue follow-up with podiatry and neurosurgery.",
