        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported that while his condition was good when not in pain, his back pain became unbearable by the end of the week while on light duty. He requested refills for Tizanidine and Meloxicam and noted he had a prior MRI of his foot and ankle. The patient had upcoming appointments with Dr. Blades and Dr. Dolce.\nObjective: Diagnoses included hypertension, low back pain, morbid obesity, right ankle pain, and smoker status.\nAssessment: Historical diagnoses included acute lumbar myofascial strain from 5/24/2023, and from 4/18/2023, a displaced fracture of the navicular in the right foot, sprains of the right ankle and right knee, and an unspecified shoulder sprain.\nPlan: The patient was prescribed acetaminophen-hydrocodone for pain as needed, acetaminophen 325 mg twice daily, and meloxicam once daily. A blood pressure machine was also prescribed.",
