        "facility": "NOMS Healthcare",
        "bodyPart": "Ankle, Foot",
        "medicineType": "Podiatry",
        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented with right foot pain following a work-related motor vehicle accident on 04/12/2023 when he rear-ended another vehicle. He reported no prior foot or ankle issues. Pain was rated 8/10 despite conservative therapies like immobilization, physical therapy, and bracing. He denied systemic symptoms such as fever, chills, low back pain, or systemic arthritis.\nObjective: Physical examination of the right ankle revealed mild circumferential swelling at the lateral malleolus. There was pain with resisted inversion and eversion of the ankle at the peroneal brevis tendon and mild tenderness over the sinus tarsi. Pulses and sensation were intact. An MRI demonstrated a longitudinal split tear of the peroneal brevis tendon in the right lateral ankle.\nAssessment: Peroneal tendon rupture, right ankle; Other synovitis and tenosynovitis, right ankle and foot.\nPlan: Due to the failure of conservative care, surgical repair and tubularization of the peroneal brevis tendon with synovectomy was recommended. The patient was instructed to remain immobilized in a brace. A worker's compensation claim was submitted for surgical approval, with a follow-up planned in two weeks.",
