        "summary": "Preoperative Diagnosis: Partial rupture peroneus brevis tendon right, synovitis peroneus brevis tendon right, and subluxation of peroneal tendon right.\nPostoperative Diagnosis: Partial rupture peroneus brevis tendon right, synovitis peroneus brevis tendon right, and subluxation of peroneal tendon right.\nProcedure: Repair of rupture peroneus brevis tendon right, synovectomy peroneus brevis tendon, and regrooving of the peroneal groove.\nAnesthesia: General.\nEstimated Blood Loss: Minimal.\nComplications: None.\nPatient's home medications included gabapentin, lisinopril, meloxicam, metoprolol succinate ER, and tizanidine.",
