        "medicineType": "Podiatry",
        "recordType": "Operative Report",
        "summary": "The patient underwent a right repair of a ruptured peroneal tendon with synovectomy and regrooving of the peroneal groove. Preoperative and postoperative diagnoses were partial rupture of the peroneus brevis tendon, synovitis of the peroneus brevis tendon, and subluxation of the peroneal tendon, all on the right. The procedure was performed under general anesthesia with minimal blood loss and no complications. The patient had provided consent for anesthesia prior to the procedure. Preoperative antibiotics were administered, and intraoperative medications included bupivacaine and lidocaine. Postoperative orders included ice, elevation, and non-weight bearing status on the operative extremity with a post-operative shoe.",
