        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for evaluation of low back pain related to a work truck accident on 04/12/2023, when another semi pulled in front of him, causing a collision. He reported injuring his left shoulder, low back, right leg, right knee, and right ankle in the accident. The patient stated he had no back pain prior to this incident and that physical therapy from June-July 2023 provided no improvement. He described significant low back pain radiating to his buttocks and down his left leg to the foot, with pain being worse on the left side and exacerbated by sitting, walking, and bending.\nObjective: The patient had difficulty moving from a sitting to a standing position and was using a knee cart due to a recent right ankle surgery. Examination revealed significant pain over the left sacral sulcus and reproduced left SI joint pain with Faber, leg thrust, and Gaenslen maneuvers. Motor strength was 5/5 in the lower extremities where tested. A review of a 06/07/2023 lumbar spine MRI showed an L4 central/left paracentral disc herniation and a left foraminal disc herniation at L5 causing moderate foraminal narrowing. A CT scan showed lumbar spondylosis at L4-S1.\nAssessment: Back strain; Lumbar herniated disc; Bilateral sacroiliitis, left worse than right.\nPlan: Order bilateral hip and pelvis x-rays; Recommend a left SI joint injection and physical therapy for sacroiliitis. Follow-up after imaging.",
