        "summary": "Subjective: The patient was evaluated for work-related injuries including lower back strain, left shoulder sprain, bilateral knee sprains, right ankle sprain, a closed nondisplaced navicular fracture of the right foot, and synovitis of the right ankle/foot. Additional conditions impacting treatment included a lumbar herniated disc and sacroiliitis.\nObjective: The patient had not been released to full duty since 04/12/23, with an estimated full duty return date of 03/28/24. An independent medical evaluation (IME) was scheduled for 02/20/24, and a hearing for additional diagnoses was pending.\nAssessment: Allowed conditions preventing a return to full duty included lower back strain, right ankle sprain, and the right foot fracture/synovitis. The patient had not yet reached maximum medical improvement (MMI).\nPlan: Work restrictions were to continue, including no semi-truck driving, no lifting, frequent position changes, and a 4-hour workday limit. Follow-up was scheduled for 03/28/24.",
