        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for follow-up of his 04/12/23 back injury, reporting persistent lower back pain radiating down both legs. He remained off work due to a lack of light-duty options. The summary details his progression since the accident, including resolution of shoulder/knee pain, persistent back pain, and right foot/ankle pain. An 08/03/23 right ankle MRI showed chronic navicular deformity, muscle atrophy, and a peroneus brevis tear. In December 2023, he was released to light duty (4 hours/day) but his employer had no suitable tasks. He was awaiting approval for diagnoses of lumbar herniated disc and sacroiliitis.\nObjective: Exam revealed lumbar paravertebral tenderness, limited flexion to 50 degrees, and a positive straight leg raise bilaterally. Neurologic exam was normal.\nAssessment: Lumbar disc herniation, acute lumbar myofascial strain, sprains of the left shoulder, right knee, and right ankle, and a displaced right navicular fracture.\nPlan: Continue Tylenol 1000 mg q8hr, use ice/heat, and walk daily up to 20 minutes. Work restrictions were 4 hours/day with no lifting. Follow-up was scheduled in 3 months.",
