        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for evaluation of low back pain, reporting bilateral leg pain (left greater than right) with numbness and tingling into the top of the left foot and right calf. He reported the pain extended into his buttocks and legs with activity.\nObjective: The patient was slow when transitioning from a sitting to standing position. A review of a prior lumbar spine MRI from 06/07/2023 showed L4-5 and L5-S1 disc herniations and Modic endplate changes. A CT from 04/12/2023 showed mild lumbar spondylosis without fracture or dislocation.\nAssessment: Lumbar intervertebral disc displacement, sacroiliitis, and lower back strain.\nPlan: To determine the primary pain generator, a left SI joint injection was recommended. An LSO 650 brace was prescribed for spinal stability and pain management, to be worn for up to three months. Follow-up was scheduled after the injection and brace fitting. The patient signed a general consent for treatment. A medication list noted no active medications at the end of the visit.",
