        "summary": "Subjective: The patient, a 33-year-old male, presented with low back pain following a hearing a week prior. He reported bilateral leg pain, left greater than right, with numbness and tingling radiating into the top of his left foot and parts of his right calf. The patient had not participated in physical therapy since July 2023. He has a history of hypertension and morbid obesity.\nObjective: The patient moved slowly from a sitting to a standing position. A review of prior imaging was performed. An MRI from 06/07/2023 showed L4-5 and L5-S1 disc herniations with Modic endplate changes. A CT scan from 04/12/2023 showed mild lumbar spondylosis without significant facet arthropathy, fracture, or dislocation.\nAssessment: Lumbar intervertebral disc displacement; sacroiliitis; and strain of the lower back.\nPlan: A left SI joint injection was recommended to determine if it was the primary pain generator. A LSO 650 orthosis was prescribed for spinal stability and pain management, to be worn for up to three months. A caudal epidural nerve block and spine surgery were also ordered. Follow-up was planned after the injection and brace fitting.",
