        "summary": "Subjective: Patient presented with significant low back and left leg pain. He reported a left sacroiliac joint injection on 10/31/24 provided 0% pain relief, though a prior caudal epidural had been helpful for about a day. Pertinent history includes hypertension, morbid obesity, prior ankle surgery, daily smoking, and heavy alcohol use.\nObjective: Patient weighed 468 lbs with a BMI of 51.4. Review of a 06/07/2023 MRI showed L4-5 and L5-S1 degenerative disc disease with disc herniations. A CT scan from 10/14/2024 showed no significant facet arthropathy at L4-5 or L5-S1. DEXA scan was normal.\nAssessment: Lumbar strain. Pain attributed to herniated discs, with physical therapy, injections, and bracing being ineffective.\nPlan: The patient may be a candidate for L4-S1 Total Disc Arthroplasty (TDA). He was referred to a weight loss clinic for medication-guided weight loss with a goal of reducing his weight to 300-350 pounds in preparation for potential surgery. A follow-up was scheduled in 6 months with a new lumbar spine x-ray series.",
