        "medicineType": "Occupational Medicine",
        "recordType": "Work Ability Report",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient was unable to work due to pain. Cognitive, emotional, social, or behavioral barriers were noted to be interfering with expected healing.\nObjective: The provider documented that physical or health restrictions related to the allowed conditions prevented a return to a full-duty job. These restrictions were considered temporary, having started on 04/12/2023 with an estimated full-duty return-to-work date of 09/12/2025.\nAssessment: Diagnoses included lower back strain, unspecified left shoulder sprain, bilateral knee sprain, right ankle sprain, closed nondisplaced navicular fracture of the foot, synovitis/tenosynovitis of the right ankle and foot, and injury/strain of the right peroneal muscle/tendon group. The patient's recovery was not progressing as expected, and the patient had not reached Maximum Medical Improvement (MMI).\nPlan: Lyrica and Topamax were discontinued, and baclofen 10 mg three times daily as needed was started. A follow-up was scheduled in four months.",
