        "facility": "Avita Health System - Galion Hospital",
        "bodyPart": "Back, Lower Back, Buttocks, Lower Leg, Thigh",
        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for follow-up regarding lumbar spine complaints, reporting bilateral numbness and tingling in his legs, significant low back pain extending to the buttocks, posterolateral thighs, and calves bilaterally, and severe difficulty transitioning from sitting to standing, walking bent forward with a limp, and inability to stand up straight; his pain was rated 8/10 and reached 10/10 at its worst, worsening with standing, walking, bending, and activity, and improving somewhat with rest. He reported a weight loss of 100 lbs since the last visit. He was unable to work due to his symptoms. Relevant history included hypertension, morbid obesity, prior left SI joint injection (0% pain relief), caudal epidural nerve block, and ankle surgery. Social history included current daily smoking (1 pack per day), alcohol use (3+ drinks/day), caffeine use, and no exercise. Objective: On exam, the patient had significant low back pain in the bilateral paraspinous and gluteal regions, walked bent forward with a limp, was able to walk on toes and heels, and had 5/5 motor strength in bilateral lower extremities. Imaging review included lumbar spine MRI from 6/7/2023 showing L5-S1 degenerative disc disease with Modic endplate changes and moderate disc herniations, CT from 10/14/2024 showing no significant facet arthropathy, normal bone density scan, and lumbar spine x-rays showing no signs of dynamic instability. Assessment: The patient was diagnosed with strain of muscle, fascia, and tendon of lower back (S39.012A), located on the lumbar spine. Providers opined that the patient had not reached maximum medical improvement due to surgical intervention being available, and that he was a very good candidate for 2-level TDA (L4-5 and L5-S1) now that he had lost considerable weight. Plan: A new lumbar spine MRI was ordered to confirm surgical candidacy, and surgery (2-level TDA: L4/5, L5/S1) was recommended pending MRI review; risks and benefits of operative and nonoperative treatment were discussed, and the patient expressed interest in proceeding. Worker's Comp paperwork was completed.",
