        "recordType": "Pre-Operative Assessment",
        "summary": "The patient underwent a pre-operative assessment for a planned 2-level total disc arthroplasty at L4/5 and L5/S1 scheduled for 08/11/2025. His medical history was largely negative for significant past issues including blood clots, anesthesia complications, or recent illness. His activity tolerance was good at over 4 METs, but screening showed an intermediate risk for obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) with a score of 3, based on high blood pressure, BMI over 35, and male gender. Preoperative labs showed a negative MRSA screen, blood type A positive, and were significant for mildly elevated chloride (109 mmol/L), mild leukocytosis (WBC 11.9), mild anemia (Hgb 13.7), and mild neutrophilia (ANC 7.4). An ECG was performed without abnormal findings. The patient received extensive instructions on medication management, skin preparation, and post-operative care, and he verbalized understanding.",
