        "medicineType": "Anesthesiology",
        "recordType": "Anesthesia Record",
        "summary": "The patient underwent general anesthesia for a two-level lumbar total disc arthroplasty at L4/5 and L5/S1 for a lumbar herniated disc. A preoperative evaluation noted a history of benign essential hypertension, class 3 obesity, and prior surgeries including a right foot surgery and hernia repair. The patient was assessed as ASA 3 and high risk for obstructive sleep apnea, with a Mallampati III airway on exam. Anesthesia was administered from 13:08 to 18:02, and numerous medications were given, including propofol, fentanyl, and hydromorphone. Post-operatively, the patient was awake, oriented, reported mild pain, denied recall of the procedure, and had an Aldrete score of 10. The anesthesia team included CRNAs Paxton N Schwaderer and Jazmin Stokes.",
