        "summary": "During the admission on 08/11/2025, the patient underwent surgery, and family was updated that the procedure was progressing well, including work on the second level to insert a disc, and was later transported to the PACU post-operatively with monitors applied and report given to nursing staff. Preoperative ABO/RH blood typing was performed and confirmed A positive. Multiple routine and urgent laboratory tests were ordered, including CHEM 7, magnesium, calcium, CBC with platelets, protime-INR, and PTT, with most results within reference ranges except for hyperglycemia (glucose 168 mg/dL and 164 mg/dL, ref 70-100), mild thrombocytosis, neutrophilia, lymphopenia, and mild anemia. Creatinine and estimated GFR were normal, indicating preserved renal function. Coagulation studies showed mildly elevated PT (14.8 sec, ref 11.8-14.4) and normal INR/PTT. Imaging was ordered for lumbar total disc arthroplasty, but the formal report was not yet available.",
