        "summary": "CBC with differential and platelet count revealed leukocytosis (WBC 14.4, ref 3.6-11.0), mild normocytic anemia (Hgb 12.7, ref 14.0-18.0; Hct 38.9, ref 42.0-52.0), thrombocytosis (platelets 421, ref 130-400), and increased RBC distribution width (15.2, ref 11.5-14.5). The differential showed elevated absolute neutrophil (9.1, ref 1.4-6.5), lymphocyte (4.1, ref 1.2-3.4), and monocyte (1.0, ref 0.0-0.7) counts. C-reactive protein was elevated at 12.6 (ref 0-10), and erythrocyte sedimentation rate was also elevated at 28 (ref 0-15). These findings are consistent with systemic inflammation or infection. The patient was also noted to be taking nicotine patch, phentermine, probiotic, and fluconazole as of August-November 2025.",
