        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for follow-up after a two-level total disk arthroplasty (TDA) at L4/5 and L5/S1 on 08/11/2025, reporting \"relentless\" back and left thigh pain, with additional pain in both buttocks. He stated that the bottom of his surgical incision was open and leaking, and that it had reopened with drainage about 4-5 days prior. Pain was rated 8/10.\nObjective: Physical examination noted serosanguineous drainage at the bottom of the incision with some granulation tissue. A review of plain x-rays from 08/23/2025 and 05/12/2025 showed the TDA hardware appeared good with no sign of gross postoperative complication.\nAssessment: Back strain.\nPlan: The wound was cleaned and a culture swab was obtained. A Prevena dressing was applied and the patient was prescribed a 10-day course of doxycycline. Labs including CRP, sedimentation rate, WBC, and blood cultures were ordered. A follow-up was scheduled for 09/02/2025 for a wound check.",
