        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for a Prevena dressing change following lumbar total disc arthroplasty (TDA), with a history of wound opening/dehiscence that was previously culture-negative. His history was significant for hypertension and morbid obesity.\nObjective: Examination of the wound showed no surrounding erythema or purulence, only erosanguineous fluid, and the wound depth was noted to be substantially less than when previously cultured.\nAssessment: Diagnoses included back strain and status post-TDA with wound dehiscence at the lower abdominal incision, with no signs of purulent drainage or infection.\nPlan: A screening culture swab was obtained from the periumbilical skin and sent to the lab for analysis. The patient was instructed to return in 14 days for a wound check.",
