        "bodyPart": "Skin, Abdomen",
        "medicineType": "Laboratory Medicine",
        "recordType": "Lab Report",
        "summary": "Lab testing was performed on a wound culture specimen collected from the periumbilical skin of the patient on 09/02/2025, with results finalized on 09/05/2025. The wound culture demonstrated moderate growth of Klebsiella aerogenes and Enterococcus faecalis Group D, with rare white blood cells, rare squamous epithelial cells, rare gram negative rods, and rare gram positive cocci observed on gram stain. Sensitivity testing showed Klebsiella aerogenes was susceptible to ceftriaxone, imipenem, gentamicin, trimethoprim/sulfamethoxazole, levofloxacin, ertapenem, cefepime, and ceftazidime, but resistant to cefazolin and amoxicillin/clavulanic acid; Enterococcus faecalis Group D was susceptible to ampicillin, penicillin G, vancomycin, gentamicin high level, and streptomycin high level. An anaerobic culture from the same site showed only light growth and no anaerobes isolated. The patient was listed as taking lisinopril, nicotine patch, phentermine, probiotic, and fluconazole as of the end of the visit, with no medications stopped during the visit.",
        "pdfLink": "pdf",
        "painScore": 4,
        "billingAmount": 450.0,
