        "summary": "The patient presented for a laboratory visit due to a postoperative infection, unspecified type, initial encounter, as the primary diagnosis. At the end of the visit, the patient was actively taking lisinopril 40 mg daily, and several medications were discontinued at discharge, including oxyCODONE-acetaminophen, naproxen, methocarbamol, doxycycline, and nicotine patch, with the patient noted as not taking some of these medications. On 9/5/2025, new prescriptions for levofloxacin and amoxicillin-clavulanate were initiated, both for 7-day courses, and a probiotic was also prescribed but later discontinued. Laboratory studies revealed an elevated C-reactive protein (16.3 mg/L, ref 0-10), an elevated sedimentation rate (36 mm/hr, ref 0-15), and a CBC notable for leukocytosis (WBC 12.6, ref 3.6-11.0), thrombocytosis (platelets 434, ref 130-400), mild anemia (hemoglobin 13.4, ref 14.0-18.0; hematocrit 41.2, ref 42.0-52.0), and mild neutrophilia (absolute neutrophil count 7.9, ref 1.4-6.5), with other cell lines within normal limits. Comprehensive metabolic panel was within normal limits, including renal and liver function tests, electrolytes, and glucose.",
