        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for follow-up of a postoperative wound infection after lumbar disc arthroplasty on 08/11/2025. He reported ongoing but decreased gray, malodorous drainage. He denied fever, chills, nausea, or vomiting. He noted mild, improving posterior and anterior pain (5/10) with radiating left leg pain. The patient stated he did not follow up as recommended and discontinued his antibiotics (levofloxacin/Augmentin). A CT scan was still pending workman's compensation approval.\nObjective: Blood pressure was elevated at 157/100 mmHg. The patient was obese with a BMI of 48.55. Exam of the anterior abdomen revealed a deep wound with a 9cm tunnel and brownish fluid after a wound VAC was removed. No pain was noted on deep palpation of the lumbar spine.\nAssessment: Postoperative wound infection. Lab results from 09/05/2025 showed leukocytosis (12.6), thrombocytosis (434), and elevated CRP (16.3). A 09/02/2025 wound culture was positive for Klebsiella aerogenes.\nPlan: The patient was noted to be non-adherent with his naproxen and oxycodone-acetaminophen prescriptions as of this visit. Further evaluation with a CT scan was pending.",
