        "facility": "Avita Health System",
        "bodyPart": "Back, Lower Back, Spine, Abdomen, Arm, Hand",
        "medicineType": "Neurological Surgery",
        "recordType": "Operative Report",
        "summary": "Preoperative diagnosis was strain of muscle, fascia, and tendon of lower back, initial encounter, which was also the postoperative diagnosis. The patient underwent an incision and drainage (I&amp;D) of a deep posterior spine abscess with application of negative pressure wound therapy, performed by Dr. David R Lawrence. General anesthesia was administered by Darren Long, APRN-CRNA. The procedure lasted from 12:12 to 12:33. Intraoperatively, the patient received medications including fentanyl, propofol, rocuronium, and cefazolin. Oxygen was administered as needed to maintain saturation &gt;92% and was discontinued postoperatively. During the admission (09/26-09/30), the patient received multiple IV and oral antibiotics including ampicillin-sulbactam, levofloxacin, ertapenem, and piperacillin-tazobactam, along with pain management (hydrocodone-acetaminophen, methocarbamol) and other supportive medications, most of which were discontinued at discharge. The patient recovered uneventfully from anesthesia and was transferred to the PACU.",
