        "summary": "The patient was discharged after being admitted for a postoperative abdominal wound infection that failed outpatient antibiotic therapy. During admission, he underwent incision, drainage, and debridement of a subcutaneous fluid collection, with placement of a wound VAC. A CT scan on 9/24 confirmed a 5.5 x 2.2 x 4.3 cm fluid collection. He was treated with IV Zosyn and Levaquin for 10 days via a midline catheter. At discharge, his condition was stable and he was instructed on activity as tolerated with a heart healthy diet. Discharge medications included Adipex-P, Norco, Lisinopril, and Methocarbamol, while several others including Levofloxacin and Naproxen were discontinued. Follow-up was scheduled with wound care and the infusion clinic.",
