        "summary": "Subjective: Patient presented for a wound check following a two-level total disc arthroplasty (TDA) at L4-5 and L5-S1 on 08/11/2025. He reported feeling 90% better than before surgery, though he still had some low back and leg discomfort, especially with standing and walking. His worst pain since surgery was 7/10, with current worst pain at 6/10 after significant activity. His Oswestry Disability Index (ODI) was 16. The surgery was complicated by a subcutaneous abdominal wound infection and dehiscence, for which he was being followed by the wound clinic but was currently off antibiotics. He reported smoking one pack of cigarettes and consuming three or more alcoholic drinks daily.\nObjective: The patient moved from sitting to standing without difficulty and had a normal gait. A small wound opening was noted without significant erythema or drainage. Review of prior imaging from 09/24/2025 and 11/17/2025 showed the TDA prostheses in place with good motion and no gross postoperative complication.\nAssessment: Other intervertebral disc displacement, lumbosacral region (M51.27).\nPlan: Prescribed physical and/or occupational therapy. Instructed to follow up in March 2026 with a new lumbar spine x-ray series and to continue with the wound clinic.",
