        "medicineType": "Occupational Medicine",
        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported that on 4/12/23, while driving his semi at 30-35 mph, another semi pulled out in front of him, causing a collision. He denied hitting his head and initially refused ambulance transport but later went to the ER due to significant pain. He complained of constant, throbbing 10/10 pain in the lower right leg, 3-4/10 sharp left shoulder pain, and 5-6/10 throbbing low back pain. He noted his right leg, knee, and ankle hit the dashboard and steering wheel.\nObjective: The patient was in moderate distress and non-weight bearing on the right. The right knee had mild edema and pain with motion. The right ankle had significant edema and was very painful to palpation with minimal movement. Abrasions and ecchymosis were noted on the right calf and ankle. Prior imaging was noted to be negative except for a small dorsal navicular fracture in the right ankle.\nAssessment: Displaced fracture of the right navicular, left shoulder sprain, right ankle sprain, and right knee sprain.\nPlan: The patient was instructed to remain non-weight bearing on the right lower extremity. An ace wrap was applied, a referral to orthopedics was made, and prescriptions were provided for Aleve and Norco 5/325mg. He was to follow up in two weeks.",
