        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported being unable to work due to a right foot navicular fracture requiring a walking boot. He was also experiencing low back and knee pain. He was non-weight bearing on his right lower extremity while awaiting an orthopedic appointment.\nObjective: Allowed work-related conditions included closed navicular fracture of the right foot, right knee sprain, right ankle sprain, and right shoulder sprain. A low back strain was also noted as an impacting condition.\nAssessment: The patient was placed on temporary work restrictions and was unable to return to full duty. He was not at Maximum Medical Improvement (MMI). The estimated full duty return-to-work date was 05/24/2023.\nPlan: Continue wearing a walking boot, manage pain with meloxicam and Tylenol, and apply ice. A referral was sent to NOMS Access Ortho, and physical therapy was planned for the right knee sprain and lumbar strain.",
