        "medicineType": "Radiology",
        "recordType": "Imaging Report",
        "summary": "Body Part: Lumbar spine MRI without contrast. Impression: Multilevel degenerative changes were noted, most prominent at L4-L5 and L5-S1, where there were focal disc herniations. At L4-L5, there was mild interspace narrowing, degenerative disc dehydration, mild posterior hypertrophic spurring, posterior disc herniation (greatest centrally), a small extruded component extending caudad, and a moderately prominent anterior extradural defect, resulting in mild to moderate focal spinal canal stenosis without significant neural foraminal encroachment. At L5-S1, there was mild interspace narrowing posteriorly, degenerative disc dehydration, posterior disc herniation (centrally, but asymmetrically greater to the left), extruded disc extending into the inferior aspect of the left L5-S1 neural foramen, mild hypertrophic facet arthritic changes, and mild hypertrophy of ligamentum flavum, with neural foraminal stenosis on the left but a capacious spinal canal. No fracture, subluxation, or intradural lesion was seen, and the conus medullaris was unremarkable.",
