        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported injuries to his left shoulder, low back, right leg, knee, and ankle from the 04/12/23 MVA. He stated his back pain was constant (5-6/10), his right knee was 7-8/10, and his right ankle was 9-10/10. He felt physical therapy had not helped his condition and he was not working.\nObjective: Physical exam revealed tenderness across the low back, a positive straight leg raise on the left, and mild edema with tenderness of the right ankle/foot. A 06/07/23 lumbar MRI showed multilevel degenerative changes with disc herniations at L4-L5 and L5-S1, resulting in mild to moderate spinal canal stenosis.\nAssessment: Diagnoses included displaced right navicular fracture, sprains of the right knee, right ankle, and shoulder, and acute lumbar myofascial strain. Additional diagnoses of L4-L5 and L5-S1 disc herniation and spinal stenosis were added based on MRI findings.\nPlan: The patient was advised to continue his medications and was referred for a right ankle MRI, podiatry, neurosurgery, and pain management. He was cleared for light-duty work with restrictions starting 07/12/23, with a follow-up scheduled in 4 weeks.",
