        "recordType": "Report",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported being unable to drive a truck due to injuries from the work-related MVA where a semi pulled out in front of his semi. He could sit for one hour before needing to move and had lifting restrictions.\nObjective: The patient's allowed conditions included a closed navicular fracture of the foot, knee sprain, ankle sprain, shoulder sprain, and lower back strain. Additional diagnoses included L4-L5 disc herniation, L4-L5 spinal canal stenosis, and L5-S1 disc herniation.\nAssessment: Work status was deemed temporary with an estimated full duty return-to-work date of 08/08/2023. Functional capacity was limited to 4 hours per day and 20 hours per week.\nPlan: Referrals were made to podiatry, neurosurgery, and pain management. An MRI of the ankle was also ordered.",
