        "summary": "Body Part: Right ankle and right foot MRI without contrast. Impression: No acute osseous findings were identified. There was a chronic appearing deformity of the dorsal navicular, diffuse muscle atrophy especially of the plantar midfoot, and longitudinal split type tearing involving the peroneus brevis tendon. Additional findings included mild distal Achilles tendinosis without tear, intact extensor and medial flexor tendons, and preserved cartilage in the tibiotalar, subtalar, and midfoot joints. There was a physiologic quantity of joint fluid, no evidence for acute fracture, osteochondral lesion, or osteomyelitis, and mild degenerative changes of the first MTP joint without significant joint effusion. The plantar aponeurosis, sinus tarsi, tarsal tunnel, flexor and extensor tendons, plantar plates, intermetatarsal spaces, and Lisfranc ligament were all within normal limits or intact, and no other significant abnormality was noted.",
