        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Independent Medical Examination",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient recounted being injured on 04/12/2023 in a semi-truck collision, causing immediate pain to his 'whole right side,' specifically his right ankle, right shoulder, and back. He described a course of care including an initial ER visit, occupational health, physical therapy for his back and leg which was unhelpful, two podiatrists (one of whom performed surgery), and a neurosurgeon who recommended injections and more PT that was not authorized. Current complaints included pain at the top of the buttocks radiating down both legs (left worse than right), exacerbated by sitting and long walks. He denied any history of back problems prior to the incident.\nObjective: Physical examination revealed a slow, wide-based gait, diffuse low back tenderness, and limited lumbar motion to 10 degrees in flexion and lateral bending. Straight leg raise was negative to 90 degrees, producing only back pain. Records reviewed included a 10/17/2023 note from Dr. Siegal referencing an MRI showing L4-5 and L5-S1 disc herniations and bilateral sacroiliitis, and a 07/18/2023 IME by Dr. McDaniel who opined the disc herniations were not clearly related to the injury. The 06/07/2023 lumbar MRI report noted multilevel degenerative changes with focal disc herniations at L4-5 and L5-S1 causing mild-to-moderate central stenosis and left neural foraminal stenosis, respectively.\nAssessment: Dr. Glazer opined that the patient has degenerative disc disease and all lumbar MRI findings are degenerative, not causally related to the work injury. He stated there was no clinical evidence of radiculopathy or sacroiliitis. He concluded the allowed condition of low back strain had reached maximum medical improvement (MMI).\nPlan: Further treatment such as SI joint injections or physical therapy was deemed not reasonable or necessary. Dr. Glazer recommended only a home exercise program and opined the patient could return to his former job without restrictions for the allowed conditions.",
