        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Independent Medical Examination",
        "summary": "Following a review of all available medical records, the examiner, Dr. Glazer, rendered an opinion within a reasonable degree of medical certainty. He acknowledged the recently added allowed conditions of ruptured right peroneal tendon, synovitis and tenosynovitis of the right ankle/foot, and subluxation of the right tarsal foot, stating they did not change his prior opinions. Dr. Glazer concluded that the patient had reached maximum medical improvement (MMI) for the allowed conditions of sprain of the right ankle, left shoulder, and right knee; low back strain; displaced dorsum navicular of the right foot; ruptured right peroneal tendon; synovitis and tenosynovitis of the right ankle/foot; and subluxation of the right tarsal foot.",
