        "summary": "Subjective: The patient reported his injuries stemmed from a motor vehicle accident on 04/12/2023 when another semi pulled out in front of him. His allowed work-related conditions included lower back strain, left shoulder sprain, right knee sprain, right ankle sprain, right foot navicular fracture, right ankle/foot synovitis/tenosynovitis, and right peroneal muscle/tendon injury. Additional conditions of lumbar herniated disc and sacroiliitis were noted to impact treatment.\nObjective: The patient was noted to have ongoing physical restrictions related to the allowed conditions. Restrictions had been in place since 04/12/2023.\nAssessment: The provider, CNP Ames, opined that the patient's recovery was progressing slower than expected, and that the patient had not reached Maximum Medical Improvement (MMI). The provider stated that the allowed conditions combined with lumbar herniation and sacroiliitis were temporary and totally disabling, but also indicated the allowed conditions alone were not the independent cause of the temporary total disability. She also noted that while the patient had reached MMI for his back, shoulder, and knee sprains, his lumbar herniation was still contributing to his disability.\nPlan: Patient had a hearing scheduled for 04/09/2024 and a follow-up appointment on 04/10/2024. He was not released to full duty.",
