        "recordType": "Operative Report",
        "summary": "Preoperative diagnosis was lumbar disk herniation and postoperative diagnosis remained lumbar disk herniation. The procedure performed was a caudal epidural nerve block with epidural fluorogram and use of fluoroscopy. The patient was placed prone, the back and buttock were prepped and draped, and local anesthesia with 1% lidocaine was administered; a 20-gauge spinal needle was inserted into the caudal epidural space, and after confirming no CSF or blood, 20 mL of 1% lidocaine and 80 mg of Depo-Medrol were injected, followed by 10 mL of lidocaine 1% into the subcutaneous tissue. The patient tolerated the procedure well and was taken to the recovery room in stable and satisfactory condition.",
