        "summary": "Body Part: Lumbar spine (CT without contrast). Impression: 1. The image quality was significantly degraded secondary to increased patient habitus and beam hardening artifact, resulting in the spinal canal being completely obscured. 2. There was no compression fracture or subluxation. 3. There was moderate multilevel degenerative facet arthropathy throughout the lumbar spine with prominent facet osteophytes, as well as moderate degenerative disc disease with disc space narrowing at L4-L5 and L5-S1. 4. Disc space narrowing and osteophytes resulted in asymmetric left foraminal stenosis at L5-S1; disc herniations at L4-L5 and L5-S1 were only demonstrated on prior MRI, and the reader was referred to the prior MRI for details on spinal canal and foraminal stenosis.",
