        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: The patient presented for a follow-up on his back pain, reporting a recent left SI joint injection on 10/31/24 provided 0% pain relief. In contrast, a prior caudal epidural was very helpful for about one day. His chief complaint was back pain following a work-related MVA.\nObjective: The patient's weight was recorded as 468 lbs with a BMI of 51.4. A prior lumbar spine MRI from 06/07/2023 showed L4-5 and L5-S1 degenerative disc disease with Modic endplate changes and disc herniations. A CT scan from 10/14/2024 showed no significant facet arthropathy at those levels, and a DEXA scan was normal.\nAssessment: Diagnosis was back strain. The provider opined that the patient's herniated discs were causing his significant low back and leg discomfort. Given the failure of physical therapy, injections, and bracing, the patient may be a candidate for L4-5 and L5-S1 total disc arthroplasty (TDA).\nPlan: The patient was referred to the Avita weight loss clinic for medication-guided weight loss in preparation for potential surgery. The goal is to reduce his weight to 300-350 pounds to determine his candidacy for a 2-level TDA. A follow-up was scheduled in 6 months with a new series of lumbar spine x-rays.",
