        "summary": "Subjective: The patient was unable to work due to pain. Previous medications, Lyrica and Topamax, were discontinued per the weight loss clinic, and Baclofen 10 mg three times daily as needed was initiated for pain. A health and behavioral assessment was planned to evaluate barriers to recovery.\nObjective: The allowed work-related conditions preventing a full-duty return to work were lower back strain, unspecified left shoulder sprain, knee sprain, right ankle sprain, closed nondisplaced navicular fracture of the right foot, synovitis/tenosynovitis of the right ankle/foot, and injury/strain to the peroneal muscle group of the right lower leg.\nAssessment: The patient was not at maximum medical improvement (MMI). Temporary restrictions were in place, beginning 04/12/2023, with an estimated full-duty return-to-work date of 09/12/2025. The patient was deemed unable to participate in vocational rehabilitation at that time.\nPlan: Baclofen was started for pain. A follow-up appointment was scheduled for 09/12/2025.",
