        "medicineType": "Orthopedic",
        "recordType": "Encounter Note",
        "summary": "Subjective: Patient reported significant low back pain extending to the buttocks, posterolateral thighs, and calves bilaterally since his work injury. Pain reached 10/10 at its worst, aggravated by standing, walking, and bending, with some improvement with rest. He stated he was unable to work due to his symptoms.\nObjective: Lumbar spine x-rays showed no dynamic instability, a CT from 10/14/2024 showed no significant facet arthropathy, and a bone density scan was normal.\nAssessment: The provider opined the patient had not reached maximum medical improvement and was a very good candidate for a 2-level total disc arthroplasty at L4-5 and L5-S1 following weight loss.\nPlan: A new lumbar spine MRI was recommended to confirm surgical appropriateness. The patient wished to proceed with surgery pending MRI results, and Worker's Compensation paperwork was completed.",
