        "medicineType": "Radiology",
        "recordType": "Imaging Report",
        "summary": "Body Part: Lumbar Spine\nIndication: Low back pain\n\nComparison: MRI from 06/07/2023\n\nFindings: Review of the MRI from 06/10/2025 revealed increased degenerative changes at L4-5 with Modic endplate changes and a slightly larger centrally located disc herniation causing bilateral neural foraminal narrowing. The L5-S1 disc degeneration also increased, with the left L5-S1 disc herniation causing increased left neuroforaminal narrowing.\n\nImpression: Progression of degenerative disc disease at L4-5 and L5-S1. Based on these findings, a two-level total disc arthroplasty (TDA) at L4-5 and L5-S1 was recommended.",
