        "summary": "Lab testing was performed on September 5, 2025, in the context of a postoperative infection diagnosis, with the patient scheduled for follow-up in Infectious Diseases with Nancy F Crum, MD. C-reactive protein was elevated at 16.3 mg/L (reference range 0-10 mg/L), indicating inflammation or infection. Sedimentation rate was also elevated at 36 mm/hr (reference range 0-15 mm/hr), further supporting an inflammatory process. Comprehensive metabolic panel results were within normal limits, including glucose, BUN, creatinine, sodium, potassium, chloride, calcium, total protein, albumin, bilirubin, AST, alkaline phosphatase, CO2, A/G ratio, ALT, and estimated GFR, with no evidence of metabolic derangement or kidney dysfunction. CBC showed leukocytosis (WBC 12.6 x10^3/uL, ref 3.6-11.0), mild thrombocytosis (platelet count 434 x10^3/uL, ref 130-400), and elevated absolute neutrophil count (7.9 x10^3/uL, ref 1.4-6.5), consistent with infection or inflammation; hemoglobin and hematocrit were slightly below reference ranges, but not markedly abnormal. All tests were performed at Galion Community Hospital, Galion, Ohio.",
