        "summary": "Pre- and post-procedure note (#563224312) for right C4/5 selective nerve block and left subcostal injection, performed by Richard Rosenquist, MD with fellow Laura N. Deschamps, DO. Subjective: neck pain radiating to the right shoulder, aching and constant, intensity 10/10, plus left-sided stabbing subcostal rib pain; BP 175/86. Procedure 1 - left subcostal injection at the 11th rib costochondral junction under fluoroscopy with lidocaine 1%, ropivacaine 0.5% 2 mL, and Depo-Medrol 20 mg. Procedure 2 - right-sided selective diagnostic C4/5 nerve block: 25-gauge needle advanced to the C4/5 neural foramen under fluoroscopy, Omnipaque contrast confirming spread from C3 to C5, then 1 mL ropivacaine 0.5% injected; no complications, no sedation. Pre/post diagnoses: foraminal stenosis of cervical region (primary), costochondritis, rib injury, costochondral pain. Post-procedure pain 3/10, alert and oriented x3. Plan: keep a pain diary, RTC as needed. Attending Rosenquist supervised all aspects.",
