        "summary": "32 y/o male driver rear-ended by a semi-truck (then a second semi-truck) while driving a truck with trailer back to work; seatbelt on, airbags deployed. Ambulated on scene, arrived by EMS in hard cervical collar and backboard. CC: left neck, left shoulder and back pain 4/10, worse with movement; denies CP, SOB, head strike, LOC. Exam: midline cervical-spine tenderness and left cervical paraspinal tenderness, tenderness over left ribs and left knee, initial bilateral LE weakness (unable to raise left leg off bed due to discomfort), neurovascularly intact, sensation intact, A&Ox4. Peripheral pulse 58 (low). CT head, CT cervical spine and CT lumbar spine ordered; Percocet given. On reevaluation improved LLE ROM, ambulatory, stable. Imaging: CT c-spine and lumbar unremarkable; CT head no acute intracranial findings with left sphenoid sinus disease. Diagnoses: MVC restrained driver, lumbar strain, cervical strain. Discharged home with work restrictions (no lifting), Rx Norco, cyclobenzaprine, ibuprofen; follow up with AultWorks and on-call spine physician. Scribed by Hannah Dugan/Hannah Simon.",
